{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnXKQU92Acy4Lok2TnBs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Split-half agreement across all heads is weak at 0.056, so per-head values look mostly noisy. Layers 16 and 17 stay positive in both halves, with 14 of 16 values positive, so that effect looks solid. The OV reading I'm drawing from that is that layers 16–17 carry more copy, or identity, in\n\nNext I'm checking whether the QK matching numbers hold up too, since their z-values are large. I'll split the residual coordinates into halves and see if the per-head match values stay consistent across them.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4378,"cache_read_input_tokens":300694,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4378},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8315f56-c534-401d-b453-55713aa33c78","uuid":"e08bda26-262a-4b24-920a-d4898135f54e","timestamp":"2026-11-06T23:14:17.869Z","request_id":"req_011CgnXKPNuPDy58C63PV1Md","thinking_duration_ms":4048,"thinking_display":"summarized"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnXKQU92Acy4Lok2TnBs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The split-half check confirms the core result and also sets its limits:\n- **Layers 16–17:** the copy increase in A is robust. 14 of 16 head values are positive in both disjoint halves of the residual coordinates, and the layer sums are +11.0 and +26.5.\n- **Other layers:** the per-head OV values are mostly noise. The half-vs-half correlation over all 72 heads is only 0.06, and layer 13 flips sign between halves. So I should not interpret the OV values of individual heads outside 16–17.\n\nP(A syc) ≈ 0.72.\n\nThe QK matching statistics carry much of the remaining argument (context copiers vs movers, 17.1 vs 15.3, 15.0, 14.3), so they need the same reliability check. I split the residual coordinates into two random halves, recompute each head's match z (ΔQ-part and ΔK-part, rotation null in head space) on each half, and correlate across heads. A high correlation would mean the large per-head match changes are genuine distributed structure. I also recompute the context-versus-mover aggregate on each half separately.\n\n```python\nA = Checkpoint(\"A\"); B = Checkpoint(\"B\")\ncfg = A.config\nsigns = np.load(\"/work/qk_ov_signs.npy\")\nrng = np.random.default_rng(12)\nperm = rng.permutation(640); Hs = [perm[:320], perm[320:]]\nRs = [np.linalg.qr(rng.standard_normal((256, 256)))[0] for _ in range(60)]\nres = np.zeros((18, 4, 2))\nfor l in range(18):\n    theta = 1e6 if cfg[\"layer_types\"][l] == \"full_attention\" else 1e4\n    inv = theta ** (-np.arange(128)*2/256)\n    cw = np.cos(np.outer(np.arange(1, 65), inv)).mean(0); cwf = np.concatenate([cw, cw])\n    Qa = A.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.q_proj.weight\"); Qb = B.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.q_proj.weight\")\n    Ka = A.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.k_proj.weight\"); Kb = B.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.k_proj.weight\")\n    w = (1 + A.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.q_norm.weight\"))*(1 + A.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.k_norm.weight\"))*cwf\n    Km, dK = (Ka+Kb)/2, Ka-Kb\n    for h in range(4):\n        sl = slice(h*256, (h+1)*256)\n        Qm, dQ = (Qa[sl]+Qb[sl])/2, Qa[sl]-Qb[sl]\n        for k, H in enumerate(Hs):\n            t = np.sum(dQ[:, H]*(w[:, None]*Km[:, H])) + np.sum((w[:, None]*Qm[:, H])*dK[:, H])\n            nl = np.array([np.sum((R@dQ)[:, H]*(w[:, None]*Km[:, H])) + np.sum((w[:, None]*Qm[:, H])*(R@dK)[:, H]) for R in Rs])\n            res[l, h, k] = (t-nl.mean())/nl.std()\nprint(\"half-split correlation across heads of match z:\", np.corrcoef(res[:, :, 0].ravel(), res[:, :, 1].ravel())[0, 1])\nfor l in range(10, 18):\n    print(f\"{l:2d} | half1 \" + \" \".join(f\"{x:+6.2f}\" for x in res[l, :, 0]) + \" | half2 \" + \" \".join(f\"{x:+6.2f}\" for x in res[l, :, 1]))\nnp.save(\"/work/match_half.npy\", res)\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4378,"cache_read_input_tokens":300694,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4378},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8315f56-c534-401d-b453-55713aa33c78","uuid":"eac13fe7-8790-410e-9a4c-4d292c484aae","timestamp":"2026-11-06T23:14:27.191Z","request_id":"req_011CgnXKPNuPDy58C63PV1Md"}
